    { "chapter": "module", "symbols": ["module.findPackageJSON"], "status": "partial", "evidence": ["tests/corpus/module-find-package-json/main.ts", "packages/compiler/test/find-package-json.test.ts"], "reason": "The lookup is resolved at build time for a string-literal specifier and a static base (import.meta.url, __filename, or a path or file: URL literal): a bare specifier answers its package's root package.json through a self-reference or the node_modules chain, and a relative or absolute specifier answers the nearest package.json after the same URL resolution Node's default resolver performs, including its trailing-separator rule for directories. A runtime-computed specifier or base is refused, and a lookup Node would reject (a missing package or file, an invalid package name, a non-file URL) keeps a named refusal." },
